& [PreservedUserIntent]
  + [verbatim_1] "could Cantor become a tool used by OpenAI Codex then? that would make it extremely useful. it's an inference co-processor."
  + [verbatim_2] "the lightest-weight operation we can configure? the slim SOP primer telling the inference to use the SOP query tool under conditions as SOP guides"
  + [verbatim_3] "I want to have a runtime environment for Cantor to interface with Codex, sending messages and taking responses."
  + [current_goal] expose the user-testable Speak Into Order path without requiring callers to reconstruct Cantor internals

& [Purpose]
  + expose completed lexical anchor lookup and admitted source quotation as one small read-only MCP tool for Codex and other MCP-capable hosts
  + let tool discovery describe when to call the operation and let strict JSON arguments name only ordinary text finite result bounds and source inclusion
  + preserve the existing supervisor-bound query_sop tool and direct protocol unchanged

& [ToolIdentity]
  + [name] lookup_sop_anchors
  + [title] Lookup signed SOP anchors
  + [annotations] read_only true destructive false idempotent true open_world false
  + [availability] embedded-environment Cantor MCP mode only because resident service does not yet carry the lexical catalogue sidecar
  + resident mode lists only query_sop and does not advertise an operation it cannot execute

& [Input]
  + text is required nonblank ordinary UTF-8 and bounded by the existing lexical query hard cap
  + include_source defaults true and requests the completed Slice4B2B projection when true
  + maximum_postings and maximum_matches are optional positive values within existing hard caps and conservative defaults
  + unknown fields malformed values and oversized encoded argument objects refuse as MCP tool errors

& [Execution]
  + embedded MCP startup preflights and admits one supplied signed runtime environment
  + prepare one immutable process-local SemanticFabric catalogue and lexical sidecar once at startup rather than rebuilding them on every call
  + each call derives a request identity from exact input text and executes completed Slice4B2A lookup
  + when requested each call executes completed Slice4B2B admitted source projection
  + return the exact structured machine result plus only a short human summary
  + no model call prompt mutation attention effect filesystem write network request background service or authority minting occurs

& [Output]
  + structuredContent binds adapter profile environment digest lexical lookup result and optional source projection
  + success is byte-repeatable for equal server generation and arguments
  + source projection is present by default and absent only when the caller explicitly sets include_source false
  + faults are closed structured MCP errors with bounded stage kind and detail

& [Compatibility]
  + query_sop name input schema output schema behavior direct equivalence and resident behavior remain byte-stable unless unavoidable metadata list ordering is explicitly accounted
  + existing MCP process command remains cantor-mcp --environment PATH or --service-config PATH
  + embedded list_tools returns query_sop then lookup_sop_anchors in fixed order
  + resident list_tools and get_tool expose query_sop only

& [Acceptance]
  + metadata is bounded strict and correctly annotated
  + embedded direct adapter and real stdio MCP process return exact signed source quotation for fixture and tracked self-hosted corpus
  + repeated calls return equal structured content
  + include_source false omits projection without changing lookup proof
  + bad arguments and resident attempt refuse without fallback or invented scope
  + focused debug release complete workspace warnings-denied Clippy format evidence diff and existing query_sop equivalence gates pass

& [Locked]
